 "post": {
  "title": "GitLab patched a flaw rated 10 out of 10",
  "caption": "GitLab patched a flaw rated 10 out of 10. 🚨\n\nCVE-2026-110264 is an integer overflow in GitLab's regular expression compiler: a crafted pattern can let someone run code on a self-hosted GitLab server without logging in. GitLab.com and GitLab Dedicated are already patched. The fixes shipped 21 Oct: 19.5.1, 19.4.3, 19.3.6, 19.2.9, 19.1.9, 19.0.10 and 18.11.13. There's no workaround, and servers on the 12 Oct patch are still exposed. Check your version and upgrade today.\nSend this to whoever runs your GitLab.",
